        "description": "<img src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/batman-begins_shUnLpR.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp\" /> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/warner-bros-reportedly-cancels-wonder-woman-closes-monolith-and-other-studios\">Monolith Productions' closure last year</a> remains one of the hardest gut punches the Western games industry has seen recently. From iconic shooters like <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/r-fear-pc\">FEAR</a> to the inventive <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/middle-earth-shadow-of-mordor-review\">Shadow of Mordor</a> & Shadow of War, the studio always excelled, no matter the genre. Now, unearthed materials allegedly recovered from a discarded HDD used at the studio have revealed work done on a non-Arkham Batman game for Warner Bros.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/monolith-productions-cancelled-2010-batman-game-new\">Read more</a></p>",
