        "description": "<img src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/ubisoft_twGFEoN.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp\" /> <p>French publisher Ubisoft is promising a nostalgic 2026, with remakes of <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/raid-shadow-legends-collaboration-assassins-creed-black-flag-remake\">Assassin&rsquo;s Creed 4: Black Flag</a> and <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/games/prince-of-persia-the-sands-of-time\">Prince of Persia: The Sands of Time</a> nearing completion, and <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/the-division-definitive-edition\">the first Division game also getting a re-release</a> of sorts. For many of the developers at key studios, however, the year is off to an awful start.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/ubisoft-continues-new-wave-of-layoffs-as-55-jobs-are-expected-to-be-cut-at-massive-and-stockholm-offices\">Read more</a></p>",
