        "description": "<img src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/stellar-blade-2_ePmcRqr.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp\" /> <p>Much has been written about <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/stellar-blade-review\">Stellar Blade</a>'s handling of its lead female character, the culture war surrounding it, and <a href=\"https://www.nme.com/news/gaming-news/stellar-blade-cuts-unintentional-reference-to-racial-slur-3750534\">developer Shift Up's several eyebrow-raising missteps</a> as the game broke through into mainstream consciousness. Regardless, the PS5 title was a big success and <a href=\"https://www.ign.com/articles/stellar-blade-developer-confirms-sequel-plans\">a sequel is now in development</a>. Before we even get a first look at it, however, a new storm appears to be brewing.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/stellar-blade-director-goes-all-in-on-ai-as-south-koreas-games-industry-looks-to-compete-on-the-global-stage\">Read more</a></p>",
